# Files consumed by bash or line-diffed by the contract tests must be LF on EVERY
# platform - including the Windows CI runner, where git's autocrlf would otherwise
# check them out as CRLF and break (a) bash scripts run under Git Bash and (b) the
# contract test's line-by-line diff of .columns against the script's $COLS array.
# PowerShell .ps1 are left native (CRLF on Windows) - they are not line-diffed.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.columns   text eol=lf
*.tsv       text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
